[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue on subject lines alone
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). Placed by tenant and booking form with
`causeOf()`, its reports split into two causes. Each now has a ticket of its own.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. The parser fix queued for #4471 does not reach the booking-v3 form reports.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The row the table marks "no ticket of its own" is
[robohere/mega_courses#2](https://github.com/robohere/mega_courses/issues/2).

## The tickets

- **`parser`**: [robohere/mega_courses#1](https://github.com/robohere/mega_courses/issues/1).
  The shared parser reads every date month first; every tenant here writes the day first.
  Day and month come out swapped, in the app, by email and through booking-v2 forms.
- **`hint`**: [robohere/mega_courses#2](https://github.com/robohere/mega_courses/issues/2).
  booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month first, as told, and
  the form reads the tenant's way, day first. Only form reports from booking-v3 tenants.

## How to read the counts

- The export pages overlap: a report can come twice. Counts are by report id.
- Intake's tag (`parser` / `hint`) is a guess from the reporter's browser. It disagrees with
  the cause in both groups; place reports by tenant, not by tag.
- The reports the desk read as a one-day move stay under `parser`, where they are filed by
  tenant (footnote under the table).

